Location: app/assets/stylesheets/common/base/topic-post.scss:264-265 (RIGHT)

Converting `.small-action` to `display:flex` makes the sibling `button`'s `float: right` layout ineffective

Trigger: Rendering a 'small action' post (e.g. moved/edited notice) whose action `button` is a direct child of `.small-action`; the unchanged `button { float: right; }` rule further down still relies on floating for right-alignment.

Impact: Per the CSS Flexbox spec, `float` on a flex item is computed as `none`, so the action `button` no longer sticks to the far right of the row; instead it renders immediately after `.small-action-desc` in normal flex order, shifting the button's position and changing the small-action layout.

Evidence: @include flexbox();
  @include align-items(center);

Suggested fix: Add `margin-left: auto;` to the `button` rule (or `justify-content: space-between;` on `.small-action`) so the button is still pushed to the far right under the new flex layout.

