false_positives.candidate:
Location: app/controllers/groups_controller.rb:28-34 (RIGHT)

Changed members.json response shape has no controller spec coverage and stale pending spec

Trigger: Running the suite after this patch: spec/controllers/groups_controller_spec.rb still contains only the old pending pagination example that parses the body as a flat array (`members = JSON.parse(response.body); members.map{ |m| m['username'] }`), which no longer matches the new {members:, meta:} envelope, and no active spec asserts the new pagination/meta behavior.

Impact: The breaking response-format change and the now-universal limit/offset behavior of GroupsController#members ship untested; the pending spec would fail if ever enabled, and regressions in total/limit/offset math would go undetected.

Evidence: render json: {
      members: serialize_data(members, GroupUserSerializer),
      meta: {
        total: total,
        limit: limit,
        offset: offset
      }
    }

Suggested fix: Update spec/controllers/groups_controller_spec.rb: un-pend and rewrite the pagination example against the new {members, meta} format, asserting total, limit, and offset values.

