Location: testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/webauthn/passwordless/PasskeysUsernamePasswordFormTest.java:291-296 (RIGHT)

Broad catch(Exception) around negative webauthn-form assertion masks unrelated test failures

Trigger: Any exception other than NoSuchElementException thrown inside the try block during reauthenticationOfUserWithoutPasskey (e.g. StaleElementReferenceException, WebDriverException, page-load timing issues); the same pattern is duplicated at R312-R317.

Impact: The negative assertion 'webauthn button is absent' passes on any driver failure, not only on the intended NoSuchElementException, so a broken page or driver error is silently treated as success and the test loses its ability to detect regressions. The `assertThat(..., nullValue())` is also dead code because findElement never returns null.

Evidence: try {
                MatcherAssert.assertThat(driver.findElement(By.xpath("//form[@id='webauth']")), nullValue());
                fail("Not expected to have webauthn button");
            } catch (Exception nsee) {
                // expected
            }

Suggested fix: Replace the try/catch with `Assert.assertThrows(NoSuchElementException.class, () -> driver.findElement(By.xpath("//form[@id='webauth']")))`, as done by the pre-existing tests in this suite.

