Location: packages/features/bookings/lib/handleNewBooking.ts:737-741 (LEFT)

loadUsers refactor drops the organization slug from the dynamic-booking user query

Trigger: A dynamic group booking (no eventTypeId) is created for users belonging to an organization; loadUsers now selects only userSelect fields, credentials, and metadata.

Impact: Downstream code that previously relied on `user.organization.slug` for dynamic bookings (e.g., org-scoped booker URLs/usernames) receives undefined, producing incorrect links or behavior for organization users.

Evidence: organization: {
              select: {
                slug: true,
              },
            },

Suggested fix: Re-add `organization: { select: { slug: true } }` to the prisma select in the !eventTypeId branch, or verify and document that no consumer reads user.organization after loadUsers.

Location: packages/features/bookings/lib/handleNewBooking.ts:1077-1079 (RIGHT)

Team hosts' destination calendars are silently dropped when the organizer has none

Trigger: A collective team booking where neither the event type nor the organizer has a destination calendar (evt.destinationCalendar is initialized to `null` at R1067) but other hosts do have destination calendars.

Impact: `?.push` on null is a no-op, so all collected teamDestinationCalendars are discarded; secondary hosts do not receive calendar events, which is the exact scenario this PR intends to fix.

Evidence: if (isTeamEventType && eventType.schedulingType === "COLLECTIVE") {
    evt.destinationCalendar?.push(...teamDestinationCalendars);
  }

Suggested fix: Initialize destinationCalendar to `[]` instead of `null` in the evt construction (or assign `evt.destinationCalendar = [...(evt.destinationCalendar ?? []), ...teamDestinationCalendars]`).

