Outgoing credential-sync request carries no authentication for the remote endpoint

Trigger: Credential sync enabled; any token refresh POSTs only `calcomUserId` and `appSlug` to the configured endpoint.

Impact: The self-hoster's endpoint receives no shared secret or signature, so it cannot verify the request originated from Cal.com. Anyone who can reach the endpoint can request another user's OAuth tokens by guessing numeric user ids, unless every operator independently invents their own auth scheme.

Evidence: const response = await fetch(process.env.CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT, {
      method: "POST",
      body: new URLSearchParams({
        calcomUserId: userId.toString(),
        appSlug,
      }),
    });

Suggested fix: Include an authentication header (e.g. the CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET or an HMAC signature of the payload) on the sync request and document that the endpoint must verify it.

