false_positives.candidate:
Location: packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/addGuests.handler.ts:158-163 (RIGHT)

Calendar update uses the acting user's credentials instead of the booking organizer's

Trigger: An attendee or team admin (not the booking organizer) invokes addGuests; the handler builds EventManager from ctx.user's credentials even though the booking query already fetched booking.user.credentials.

Impact: updateCalendarAttendees runs with the caller's (often empty or unrelated) credentials, so the organizer's calendar/video event is never updated with the new guests; guests are saved in the DB but the external calendar invite stays stale.

Evidence: const credentials = await getUsersCredentials(ctx.user);

  const eventManager = new EventManager({
    ...user,
    credentials: [...credentials],
  });

Suggested fix: When the caller is not the organizer, construct EventManager from the booking owner's credentials (booking.user.credentials, already included in the query) or the destination calendar's credential.

