false_positives.candidate:
Location: apps/web/components/dialog/AddGuestsDialog.tsx:26-29 (RIGHT)

Validation schema rebuilt on every render inside the dialog component

Trigger: Every render of AddGuestsDialog (each keystroke in MultiEmail) re-executes the zod builder.

Impact: Needless per-render schema construction, and the local name shadows the unrelated server schema `ZAddGuestsInputSchema` (an object schema with bookingId), which misleads readers into thinking they are the same contract.

Evidence: const ZAddGuestsInputSchema = z.array(z.string().email()).refine((emails) => {
    const uniqueEmails = new Set(emails);
    return uniqueEmails.size === emails.length;
  });

Suggested fix: Move the schema to module scope with a distinct name (e.g. `guestEmailsSchema`) outside the component body.

Location: apps/web/components/dialog/AddGuestsDialog.tsx:36-40 (RIGHT)

Validation error state not cleared after successful add

Trigger: User submits an invalid/duplicate email (setting isInvalidEmail true), fixes it, submits successfully, then reopens the Add guests dialog for the same booking row.

Impact: `isInvalidEmail` stays true because the component stays mounted, so the reopened dialog shows the stale "Emails must be unique and valid" error with an empty form.

Evidence: onSuccess: async () => {
      showToast(t("guests_added"), "success");
      setIsOpenDialog(false);
      setMultiEmailValue([""]);
      utils.viewer.bookings.invalidate();

Suggested fix: Call `setIsInvalidEmail(false)` in the mutation's `onSuccess` (and/or when the email values change), as the cancel handler already does.

