try/catch around un-awaited reminder cancellation calls is unreachable dead code

Trigger: Any failure inside deleteScheduledEmailReminder/deleteScheduledSMSReminder during a reschedule: both functions catch all errors internally, and the calls inside forEach are not awaited, so no rejection can propagate to this try block.

Impact: The `log.error` branch can never execute; failures during reminder cancellation are silently swallowed by inner console.log catches, giving reviewers/operators a false impression that this path is monitored.

Evidence: } catch (error) {
      log.error("Error while canceling scheduled workflow reminders", error);
    }

Suggested fix: Either remove the dead try/catch, or make the delete functions rethrow/return errors and await them (e.g., `await Promise.all(...)`) so the catch can actually observe failures.

Location: packages/features/ee/workflows/api/scheduleEmailReminders.ts:53-57 (RIGHT)

Single try/catch around SendGrid cancellation loop aborts all remaining cancellations on first failure

Trigger: The CRON runs with multiple `cancelled: true` reminders pending and one SendGrid cancel request fails (e.g., expired/invalid batch referenceId, 100-pending-cancellation limit, transient API error) partway through the loop.

Impact: The catch exits the entire loop: all subsequent reminders in `remindersToCancel` are never cancelled at SendGrid in this run, and the already-pushed but not-yet-awaited PrismaPromise deletes never execute (Prisma queries only run when awaited). If the failing reminder sorts early on every run, other cancelled bookings' reminder emails are still sent once their send time passes.

Evidence: try {
    const workflowRemindersToDelete: Prisma.Prisma__WorkflowReminderClient<WorkflowReminder, never>[] = [];

    for (const reminder of remindersToCancel) {
      await client.request({

Suggested fix: Move the try/catch inside the for-loop so each reminder is cancelled/deleted independently, and await (or explicitly execute) the delete per iteration instead of deferring all deletes to a single Promise.all after the loop.

