Location: packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts:480-483 (RIGHT)

Sequential await in for...of loop serializes calendar resolution that was previously synchronous

Trigger: A booking whose user has multiple `_calendar` credentials (calendarCredentials.length > 1) needing cancellation via the legacy code path (no credentialId on the booking calendar reference).

Impact: Each credential's getCalendar (which performs a dynamic app import) is awaited before starting the next iteration, increasing total cancellation latency compared to resolving them concurrently.

Evidence: for (const credential of calendarCredentials) {
        const calendar = await getCalendar(credential);
        apiDeletes.push(calendar?.deleteEvent(uid, evt, externalCalendarId) as Promise<unknown>);
      }

Suggested fix: Use `await Promise.all(calendarCredentials.map(async (credential) => { const calendar = await getCalendar(credential); apiDeletes.push(...); }))` to resolve calendars concurrently.

