Location: services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java:100-103 (RIGHT)

New MAP_ROLES_CLIENT_SCOPE client scope has no end-to-end test coverage

Trigger: PermissionClientTest exercises MANAGE, CONFIGURE, VIEW, MAP_ROLES and MAP_ROLES_COMPOSITE, but no test grants or evaluates the newly added map-roles-client-scope scope via canMapClientScopeRoles.

Impact: A regression in the map-roles-client-scope evaluation path (e.g., wrong scope name or broken fallback to the all-clients resource) would ship undetected because the new authorization branch is untested.

Evidence: @Override
    public boolean canMapClientScopeRoles(ClientModel client) {
        return hasPermission(client, AdminPermissionsSchema.MAP_ROLES_CLIENT_SCOPE);
    }

Suggested fix: Extend PermissionClientTest with a case that grants Set.of(MAP_ROLES_CLIENT_SCOPE) on a client and verifies scope-mapping role operations succeed only after the grant.

Location: services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java:148-150 (RIGHT)

Legacy token exchange throws UnsupportedOperationException instead of denying when V2 FGAP is enabled

Trigger: The legacy token-exchange flow calls AdminPermissions.management(...).clients().canExchangeTo(...); if the token-exchange feature and ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2 are enabled together, management() returns MgmtPermissionsV2 and this override throws instead of returning false.

Impact: Token-exchange requests that previously received a clean permission denial now surface as an unhandled UnsupportedOperationException (HTTP 500), because canExchangeTo's callers are gated by the token-exchange feature, not by the V1 FGAP feature.

Evidence: public boolean canExchangeTo(ClientModel authorizedClient, ClientModel to, AccessToken token) {
        throw new UnsupportedOperationException("Not supported in V2");
    }

Suggested fix: Return false (deny) from canExchangeTo in V2, or verify every call site is unreachable when V2 is enabled and document that invariant.

