getClientsWithPermission queries by resource type that per-client resources never have, returning wrong results

Trigger: getClientsWithPermission is called after per-client permissions were created: AdminPermissionsSchema.getOrCreateResource creates per-client resources via resourceStore.create(...) without ever calling setType, so findByType(server, "Clients") matches only the umbrella "Clients" resource created in init() (which does set the type), never the per-client resources.

Impact: The method never returns the ids of individually granted clients, and if the umbrella all-clients permission is granted it adds the literal string "Clients" to a set that callers interpret as client ids, breaking client-list filtering for restricted admins.

Evidence: resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.CLIENTS_RESOURCE_TYPE, resource -> {
            if (hasGrantedPermission(resource, scope)) {
                granted.add(resource.getName());
            }
        });

Suggested fix: Set the resource type to CLIENTS_RESOURCE_TYPE when creating per-client resources in AdminPermissionsSchema.getOrCreateResource (and exclude the umbrella type resource from the result), or enumerate per-client resources by another criterion.

