Location: services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/services/resources/admin/permissions/ClientPermissionsV2.java:138-142 (RIGHT)

getClientsWithPermission returns the "Clients" resource-type resource name instead of client ids

Trigger: An administrator is granted a scope on the schema-level "Clients" resource (the all-clients resource created by AdminPermissionsSchema.init with name and type both equal to "Clients"), and a caller invokes ClientPermissionEvaluator#getClientsWithPermission (e.g. AvailableRoleMappingResource#getRoleIdsWithPermissions).

Impact: The returned set contains the literal string "Clients" instead of client UUIDs; consumers such as AvailableRoleMappingResource do `realm.getClientById(cid).getRolesStream()` and dereference null, producing a NullPointerException / 500. Additionally, per-client resources created by AdminPermissionsSchema.getOrCreateResource have no resource type set, so they are never matched by findByType and genuinely granted clients are omitted.

Evidence: resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.CLIENTS_RESOURCE_TYPE, resource -> {
            if (hasGrantedPermission(resource, scope)) {
                granted.add(resource.getName());
            }
        });

Suggested fix: Skip the resource whose name equals AdminPermissionsSchema.CLIENTS_RESOURCE_TYPE and enumerate the actual per-client resources (e.g. iterate realm clients and call hasPermission(client, scope), or set the resource type when creating per-client resources).

