Reader thread busy-loops with no pause and requests Integer.MAX_VALUE results per call

Trigger: The test runs the loop continuously for the whole duration of the 100 sequential group deletions, each iteration issuing an unbounded (`max = Integer.MAX_VALUE`) group listing request against the test server.

Impact: Unthrottled full-listing requests add significant CPU/DB load to the shared test server, slowing the suite and increasing the chance of unrelated timeouts in parallel tests.

Evidence: while (!deletedAll.get()) {
                try {
                    // just loading briefs
                    managedRealm.admin().groups().groups(null, 0, Integer.MAX_VALUE, true);

Suggested fix: Add a small sleep/back-off inside the loop and bound the page size (for example `groups(null, 0, 200, true)`) instead of `Integer.MAX_VALUE`.

